   "speech": "Precisely this same attitude towards all that exists — an attitude of musical exaltation — made up the unvarying tone of Duplay’s life. It was as though an invisible orchestra accompanied him, developing endless variations upon a certain fundamental melody, whose sounds, inaccessible to physical hearing, left an impression of the most perfect musical loveliness. By virtue of such a complication of perception, Duplay’s own person, with all that he did, thought and said, seemed visible to him as if from outside — a character in a play without title or end — an object of observation. Even sufferings, in their blackest and most tormenting degree, Duplay bore along that same road of detached impression; he himself was the audience. And the hero of the play — he was immersed in vivid contemplation, coloured by musical emotion.",
